// Practice quiz: Reading: common API security risks (OWASP)
// Minimum release, November 2026: author-checked, no independent review. Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: spring-boot/api-security/common-api-security-risks-owasp

::o1 BOLA::A user reads another user order by changing an id in the URL. Which risk is this? {
~Broken Authentication#Not quite. The user really is logged in.
=Broken Object Level Authorization#Correct. It is API1 on the 2023 list.
~Broken Function Level Authorization#Not quite. The action is allowed; the record is the issue.
~Injection#Not quite. The input is not being injected.
}

::o1 BFLA::A normal user calls an admin-only endpoint successfully. Which risk is this? {
=Broken Function Level Authorization#Correct. It is API5.
~Broken Object Level Authorization#Not quite. The issue is the action, not one record.
~Broken Authentication#Not quite. Identity is not the failing check.
~Security Misconfiguration only#Not quite. API5 names this case exactly.
}

::o1 authentication::A JWT is accepted long after expiry because no check runs. Which risk is this? {
~Broken Object Level Authorization#Not quite. It is not about one record.
~Broken Function Level Authorization#Not quite. It is not about a role.
~Excessive Data Exposure#Not quite. That is about returned fields.
=Broken Authentication#Correct. It is API2\: identity proof is weak.
}

::o2 fix::What fixes reading another user order by id? {
~A longer token#Not quite. It does not change access to records.
=Checking ownership in the query or service#Correct. The record must belong to the caller.
~A role check alone#Not quite. All customers share the same role.
~Hiding the id in the response#Not quite. Attackers can still guess ids.
}

::o3 connecting practices::Which earlier practice most reduces mass assignment? {
~Flyway#Not quite. It manages schema.
~Pagination#Not quite. It limits results.
=Request DTOs that accept only allowed fields#Correct. A client cannot set what is not bound.
~SQL logging#Not quite. It helps debugging.
}

